<title>MEXICO: Mexico Afores look to reduce costs, commissions.</title>
<headline>Mexico Afores look to reduce costs, commissions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's private pension funds are seeking mechanisms to reduce their operating and commission costs, the director of the Mexican Association of Afores, Ralf Peters Castilla, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We are very concerned over the operating costs that the Afores have, and for this reason we are studying ways of reducing costs to see if we can have lower commissions,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Mexico's new system of private pension funds, Afores, will start operating on July 1. The system has been heavily criticized for high commissions.</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9549))</p>
